# PART 9 — VERIFIED 2027 BOARD AND COMPETITIVE-EXAM COUNTDOWN

Create a dedicated examination calendar and countdown feature on the home page and dashboard.

The countdown must use real examination records, not hardcoded numbers or invented dates.

Support relevant 2027 examinations, including:

- CBSE Class 10 Board Examinations.
- CBSE Class 12 Board Examinations.
- Relevant state board examinations.
- JEE Main and JEE Advanced.
- NEET-UG.
- CUET-UG.
- Other supported competitive or entrance examinations that the student chooses.

Treat this as a configurable examination calendar, not a permanently hardcoded list.

### A. Official date verification

Retrieve examination dates from official board and examination-authority announcements whenever available.

Store the examination name, year, applicable session, start date, end date if known, official source URL, date of verification, and publication or announcement status.

Distinguish between confirmed dates, officially announced date ranges, tentative schedules, and dates that have not yet been announced.

Do not fabricate an exact date when only an approximate examination window is available.

If an official 2027 date has not been announced, display:

"Official date not announced yet."

If a reliable provisional schedule exists, label it clearly as provisional and show its source.

Update records through an authorized process when official schedules change. Preserve previous values and record the change history.

### B. Countdown display

Each examination card should display:

- Examination name.
- Applicable year and session.
- Confirmed examination date or known date range.
- Days remaining, when a valid date is available.
- Date verification status.
- A link to the official examination notice.
- An option to follow the examination.

Calculate the countdown from the current date in the relevant examination's local time zone.

Handle dates correctly across time zones and daylight-saving boundaries where relevant. For date-only examinations, calculate calendar days remaining rather than relying on arbitrary server timestamps.

When an examination date changes, recalculate the countdown automatically.

If the examination has started or finished, display the appropriate status instead of a negative countdown.

### C. Personalized examination selection

Allow students to select the examinations relevant to their goals.

A Class 10 student should be able to follow their board examination without being forced to see unrelated entrance-exam countdowns.

A Class 12 student preparing for NEET or JEE should be able to follow their board examinations and selected entrance examinations together.

Provide controls to add, remove, reorder, and prioritize followed examinations.

Save these preferences to the user's account.

# PART 10 — FUNCTIONAL EXAMINATION REMINDERS

The countdown must connect to a real reminder system.

Allow students to choose reminder intervals, such as 90, 60, 30, 14, 7, 3, and 1 day before an examination, where applicable.

Allow reminders for verified schedule changes, application deadlines, registration deadlines, admit-card announcements, and other important official milestones when those dates are available.

Do not create a reminder for an unverified deadline as if it were official.

The backend must store reminder preferences and calculate when notifications are due.

Use a reliable scheduled job or managed scheduling service to process due reminders. Prevent duplicate delivery and track success or failure.

Provide in-app notifications and support email or push notifications if the required services and permissions are configured.

Clearly communicate which notification channels are enabled. Do not claim that an email or push reminder has been sent if delivery has not been confirmed.

If a student changes their followed examinations or reminder preferences, update future reminders accordingly.

If an examination date changes or a schedule is cancelled, update or cancel affected reminders and notify the student where appropriate.

Support the student's time zone and preferred notification settings.

